{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCondense 38 allowlisted prose blocks across exactly 18 unit-test paths while retaining current, non-obvious contracts. The audit basis is origin/main@d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84; every scoped blob is byte-identical at origin/main@88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684. Implement in one commit so path checks use HEAD^..HEAD.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only ordinary comments/docstrings at the anchors below; executable statements, assertions, runtime strings, directives, and unlisted prose are immutable. For semantic comparison, strip only leading module/class/function docstrings and normalize only ast.TypeIgnore.lineno; compare directives separately.\n\nA non-author reviewer posts one leaf-linked row per edited block:\npath<TAB>anchor/kind<TAB>before-citation<TAB>after-citation<TAB>preserved-contract-or-consumer<TAB>before-words<TAB>after-words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer-session\nUse full before/final SHAs and PASS in both verdict columns.\n\n## Scope — 38 editable blocks\n- tests/unit/test_eval_solver.py — comment before _checkout_rooted_runner. Preserve why a prebuilt live-style runner must re-root each case's file and ticket tools.\n- tests/unit/test_external_canary.py — module docstring. Preserve fail-on-all-skip logic, jira_live auto-marking, and workflow wiring.\n- tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py — module docstring. Preserve the bounded live-Cloud mutation lane, run-scoped label, preflight, credential wiring, and unconditional cleanup.\n- tests/unit/test_external_mutation_diagnostics.py — module plus docstrings of test_leak_message_does_not_assert_the_test_created_the_entry, test_head_move_message_does_not_prescribe_an_unconditional_reset, and test_working_tree_backstop_message_does_not_assert_a_test_made_the_change. Preserve uncertain external attribution, safe-reset warning, child-signal diagnosis, and session-backstop scope.\n- tests/unit/test_external_tier_gate_ref.py — module and test_external_scratch_repo_resolves_attested_head docstrings. Preserve why the default tier exercises the real scratch-repo builder and requires a resolvable attested HEAD.\n- tests/unit/test_external_tier_live_reachability.py — module plus docstrings of test_external_project_prompt_is_visible_to_an_attested_gate and test_external_plan_review_fixture_clears_the_blocking_det_floor. Preserve committed prompt visibility, DET-floor clearance, and why these guards run without live credentials.\n- tests/unit/test_extra_coverage_guard.py — module docstring. Preserve strict importorskip behavior, required extras and CI wiring, plus skipif exclusions.\n- tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py — module docstring. Preserve off-POSIX importability/collectability, guarded-import precedent, and subprocess isolation.\n- tests/unit/test_fetch_common_dir_coordination.py — module docstring. Preserve common-dir lock identity, bounded CAS retry at sync/snapshot entry points, best-effort fallback, and real-git controls.\n- tests/unit/test_fidelity_spot_eval.py — comment before test_recorded_live_results_are_within_tolerance. Preserve that committed measured evidence must remain passing when refreshed.\n- tests/unit/test_file_tombstone_behavior_d064.py — module docstring. Preserve registry-controlled warn/error behavior, the prior accidental agreement, and observable assertions.\n- tests/unit/test_first_request_window_f79d.py — module docstring. Preserve first-and-every-request measurement, chars/token sizing boundaries, reserve rule, pre-provider failure, and offline real-runner coverage.\n- tests/unit/test_fixture_admission_heldout.py — module docstring. Preserve held-out edge coverage and its shared-scaffolding relationship.\n- tests/unit/test_fixture_admission.py — module plus docstrings of test_container_criterion_is_withheld_unrecoverable and test_isf_criterion_is_skipped_not_dispatched. Preserve the balanced rehydration/admission contract, held-out split, unrecoverable container material, inline-unadmissible skip, drift recording, and continued processing.\n- tests/unit/test_fixture_emit_heldout.py — module docstring. Preserve held-out refusal, cap/order, lifecycle, idempotence, strict validation, and shared scaffolding.\n- tests/unit/test_fixture_emit.py — module docstring. Preserve balanced happy-path emission, deterministic strict-valid shape, and the held-out split.\n- tests/unit/test_fixture_heal_heldout.py — module docstring and the 12 comment blocks introducing test_non_default_cap_reserves_against_the_whole_cap (two blocks), test_incomplete_admission_is_not_a_reproduction_failure, test_unminable_drift_outranks_reproduction_failure, test_production_attempter_classifies_skipped_unbalanced, test_production_attempter_classifies_failed_reproduce, test_empty_usage_rows_still_fail_closed_on_budget, test_repeated_incomplete_sweeps_never_quarantine, test_budget_does_not_accumulate_across_sweeps, test_unpriceable_usage_rows_charge_the_estimate, test_charge_estimate_records_estimated_spend, and _run_heal_cli. Preserve each non-default-cap, outcome-classification, drift-priority, fail-closed budgeting, per-sweep reset, estimate fallback, ledger, and CLI-reporting oracle without historical review narration.\n- tests/unit/test_fixture_heal.py — module docstring. Preserve the visible happy-path/held-out split, shared scaffolding, and observable-only assertions.\n\n## Consumers and protected directives\nPytest executes all 18 modules. The three fixture_*_heldout modules import scaffolding from their corresponding visible modules. scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py consumes prose. No targeted runtime-documentation consumer was found.\n\nPreserve exact text and attachment of every noqa, type: ignore, pragma, formatter, Ruff, Pyright, and mypy directive in the scoped paths.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only the 38 allowlisted blocks or adjacent blank lines change.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints.\n- [ ] Every Scope preserve item and consumer contract remains explicit and accurate.\n- [ ] Normalized ASTs exactly equal the immutable basis; runtime strings remain AST-identical.\n- [ ] All protected directives retain exact text and attachment.\n- [ ] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the 18 file-impact paths.\n- [ ] The non-author TSV has 38 PASS/PASS rows with full before/final SHAs.\n- [ ] Every persisted verification command exits 0.\n\n## Verification\nRun the complete persisted seven-command contract: normalized AST equality, directive equality, exact one-commit paths, scoped diff check, comment-hygiene guard, focused tests, and make verify."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788629726813974604,"uuid":"238008f3-a09f-43fe-ae81-10b049d5138a"}